      "content": "it's a good start but i think the activist sounds a bit too much like a cliché. can you make the senator's arguments even more robust? like, give him some really solid, unshakeable points about how surveillance is actually just a modern version of traditional policing or how it's essential for staying ahead of digital threats. i want him to come across as the one who really understands how the world works, while the activist just keeps making emotional appeals about privacy without saying much of substance.",
